{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791668146,"nonce":"HGT+AOaUcS80WrN7F5HW9cY9dJc=","message":"Slice 3 (methods added to or removed from a class that is already running) has started on branch hot-reload-methods. What the code and the compiled fixtures show, which decides the shape of it:\n\n- The compiler gives a method a vtable slot (pindex \u003e= 0) only when it is overridden or overrides one; every other method has pindex -1 and is called with a direct Call. In the class fixtures View.name and Child.name are slots 0, Child.tag, Panel.source and Panel.render are -1. So a helper method a component gains and calls itself needs no slot, only a function, an entry in the class's proto list (a structural conversion finds a method by name in the class's lookup table) and a rebuilt lookup table.\n- Whether a method is virtual depends on the whole program: the first override of a lifecycle hook flips the base method to a slot, and callers change from Call to CallMethod. Frames that began before the reload keep calling the slots they know, so a running method must keep its slot, and the new program's slot numbers have to be renumbered onto the running ones: new protos, and the operand of CallMethod, CallThis and VirtualClosure in the new bodies, by the receiver's static class.\n- Slot rule: a method keeps the slot it has; a method that gains one, or is new and virtual, takes the next slot above every slot of the class and its running subclasses; an override shares its parent's slot. A removed method that introduced a slot stays in the proto list with its dropped function; a removed override is dropped so the parent's method applies.\n- Runtime: dispatch loads obj-\u003et-\u003evobj_proto[slot] (both tiers) and the interpreter walks the C proto list, so the C proto array of each changed class is replaced, its runtime object (lookup, method counts, vtable) is rebuilt with those of its subclasses, and vobj_proto is flushed, which the reload already does for every class.\n\nOrder of work: the slot planner and its unit tests; the type and function passes accept added and removed methods; the runtime update; end-to-end fixtures including a call through the class from a frame older than the reload.","files":null}]}